\begin{align*}
x^2 + 4x + 4x \sqrt{x + 3} &= 13
\quad \Rightarrow \\
(x + 2 \sqrt{x + 3})^2 &= 13.
\end{align*}Let $y = x + 2 \sqrt{x + 3} = \pm \sqrt{13}.$  Then
$y^2 = 13$ and
\begin{align*}
(y - 2 \sqrt{x + 3})^2 &= 0\\
&= 0, & & \text{(Expanding, equating coefficients)}\\
&= 4x + 12 \sqrt{x + 3}, & & \text{(Expanding, sqrt-dealing)}.
